  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Tilak Singh vs Food Inspector Through Nagar Palika And ... on 18 November, 2019 Author: Pradeep Kumar Srivastava Bench: Pradeep Kumar Srivastava High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 55 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 1126 of 2001 Revisionist :- Tilak Singh Opposite Party :- Food Inspector Through Nagar Palika And State Of U.P.",
    "facts": "1 Aggrieved by the judgement of both the court below, this revision has been filed by the revisionist on the ground that both the court below have passed the judgement without perusing the record properly. The revisionist/convicted accused is innocent person who was falsely implicated for the purpose of harassment only. Thereafter, after dividing the said milk in three equal proportion and keeping all into three bottles, sealing and pasting level on them and taking signature of accused thereon, the said milk was sent to Public Analyst, Varanasi and in the report of analyst, it was found that in the milk there was 9% less fat and milk solid was found 20% less. On that basis, a complaint was filed and charge was framed against the accused after taking evidence of complainant and other witnesses. The witnesses were also cross examined and the statement of accused was recorded under section 313 Cr.P.C.",
